WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.382
A plan earns its keep by saying
what has to be true before

2
00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:06.425
the next step starts, not by
putting dates on a chart.

3
00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:11.575
Book 01 of the workbook is canonical:
seven phases and six gates.

4
00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:15.838
Phase 0, Pre-flight, ends
at G0, Ready to Plan.

5
00:00:15.838 --> 00:00:20.400
Phase 1, Foundation, ends
at G1, Foundation Complete.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.800
Phase 2, the pilot division,
ends at G2, Pilot Clean.

7
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.400
Phase 3, general rollout,
at G3, Rollout Complete.

8
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.812
Phase 4, legacy retirement,
at G4, Legacy Quiet.

9
00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:38.849
Phase 5, AD DS retirement,
at G5, AD Retired.

10
00:00:38.849 --> 00:00:43.000
Phase 6, steady state, runs
on a cadence indefinitely.

11
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.688
The gates are owned in
proportion to what they end.

12
00:00:45.688 --> 00:00:52.513
The steward clears G0, G1 and G4, and
co-signs G2 with the executive sponsor.

13
00:00:52.513 --> 00:00:55.676
The sponsor and steering
committee clear G3.

14
00:00:55.676 --> 00:00:58.963
The sponsor and the CIO clear G5.

15
00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:01.636
And five constraints bind every phase,

16
00:01:01.636 --> 00:01:05.312
from provenance on every
change to no rip-and-replace.

17
00:01:05.312 --> 00:01:10.187
The program's detailed master plan
sequences 48 milestones over an

18
00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:15.062
illustrative 52 weeks, but its
cutover ends with AD DS still running.

19
00:01:15.062 --> 00:01:18.850
Book 01's own fifty-two-week
sequence models a mid-size,

20
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:23.500
clean forest, and large federal
estates typically run multi-year.

21
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.071
So the decision for the sponsor
and CIO, when they accept the plan:

22
00:01:28.071 --> 00:01:32.950
budget the AD DS retirement phase on
top of the master plan's 52 weeks.
